{
  "$comment": [
    "The common envelope's cases (docs/tool-contract.md, \"Common envelope\"), stated once for every system tool",
    "and for docproc: docproc-ooxml's tests, the shared Rust crate's, docproc-mail's, and docproc's",
    "internal/cli's read this file in place, so no language restates a case. A case is added here, never in",
    "one tool's tests.",
    "exit_codes: each exit code and its meaning.",
    "warnings: a warning's where and what as the tool has them, and the stderr line it writes for them, its",
    "  tool's name spelled \"tool\"; split at its first three \": \" and unescaped, the line gives them back.",
    "errors: an error's reason and the stderr line it writes for it, its tool's name spelled \"tool\".",
    "media_names: a payload's bytes, in lowercase hex, and the name it is stored under, and the media name",
    "  they make: the bytes' lowercase hex SHA-256, then \".\" and the stored extension when that is 1 to 8",
    "  ASCII letters and digits.",
    "literal_escape: a line of literal text and its Markdown; no case holds a line break.",
    "destinations: a link's or an image's target and the Markdown destination written for it, which",
    "  CommonMark reads back as the target, or as reads where a case has one; a table cell's | is left to",
    "  the cell's writer, so no case holds one.",
    "titles: a link's or an image's title and the Markdown written for it within a title's \"…\", which",
    "  CommonMark reads back as the title, or as reads where a case has one; a table cell's | is left to",
    "  the cell's writer, so no case holds one."
  ],
  "exit_codes": [
    { "code": 0, "meaning": "read, skipped items included" },
